    "id": "d87495136c68b0fc",
    "title": "Nike overpaid $7.9 billion buying back its own stock",
    "summary": "The opportunity cost of Nike’s stock buybacks now reaches nearly $8B, and its repurchase program is on pause with $5.9B left.\nThe post Nike overpaid $7.9 billion buying back its own stock appeared first on Protos.",
    "hasSummary": true,
    "link": "https://protos.com/nike-overpaid-7-9-billion-buying-back-its-own-stock/",
    "source": "Protos",
    "tags": [
      "Nike"
    ],
    "origin": "rss",
    "pubDate": "2026-10-06T18:10:23.000Z",
    "fetchedAt": "2026-10-06T18:32:14.034Z",
    "isDuplicateOf": null,
    "content": "Nike has faced significant financial drawbacks from its stock buyback program, resulting in an estimated opportunity cost of nearly $7.9 billion. Following these massive losses, the company has decided to pause its ongoing repurchase program, leaving approximately $5.9 billion remaining in authorized funds. The situation highlights the heavy impact of poorly timed corporate stock repurchases on market capital.",
    "content_ta": "Nike நிறுவனத்தின் பங்கு வாபஸ் (stock buyback) திட்டத்தினால் சுமார் 7.9 பில்லியன் டாலர் வரை இழப்பு ஏற்பட்டுள்ளதாகக் கண்டறியப்பட்டுள்ளது. இந்த பெரும் நிதி இழப்பைத் தொடர்ந்து, மீதமுள்ள 5.9 பில்லியன் டாலர் தொகையுடன் இந்நிறுவனம் தனது பங்கு வாங்கும் திட்டத்தை தற்காலிகமாக நிறுத்தி வைத்துள்ளது.",
    "slug": "nike-overpaid-7-9-billion-buying-back-its-own-stock"
  },
